Task 2: Uninstall conflicting systemd-logger
Description Task 2: Remove the systemd-logger package to prevent conflicts with rsyslog.

Task 3: Install rsyslog
Description Task 3: Install the rsyslog package using variables rsyslog_packages and rsyslog_package_state.

Task 4: Install additional rsyslog packages
Description Task 4: Install additional rsyslog packages based on the items listed in rsyslog_features variable.

Task 5: Configuring default rsyslog
Description Task 5: Configure default rsyslog settings using the template specified in rsyslog_config_file_format and deploy to rsyslog_dest_conf_file. Notify Restart rsyslog handler.

Task 6: Make configuration directory
Description Task 6: Create the /etc/rsyslog.d/ directory with mode 0755.

Task 7: Configuring rsyslog forward rule
Description Task 7: Configure rsyslog forward rule using template forward_rule.conf.j2 and deploy to /etc/rsyslog.d/{{ rsyslog_forward_rule_name }}.conf. Notify Restart rsyslog handler. Only execute if rsyslog_deploy_default_config is false.

Task 8: Configuring additional config files
Description Task 8: Copy additional configuration files from rsyslog_rsyslog_d_files dictionary to /etc/rsyslog.d/ directory. Validate if specified. Notify Restart rsyslog handler. Only execute if item.value.state is present.

Task 9: Start and enable rsyslog
Description Task 9: Start and enable the rsyslog service using the name specified in rsyslog_service variable.


- Last generated (faulty) playbook: 
---

  - name: Import assert.yml
    include_tasks: assert.yml

  - name: Uninstall conflicting systemd-logger
    package:
      name: systemd-logger
      state: absent

  - name: Install rsyslog
    package:
      name: "{{ rsyslog_packages }}"
      state: "{{ rsyslog_package_state }}"

  - name: Install additional rsyslog packages
    package:
      name: "{{ item }}"
      state: present
    loop: "{{ rsyslog_features }}"

  - name: Configuring default rsyslog
    template:
      src: "{{ rsyslog_config_file_format }}"
      dest: "{{ rsyslog_dest_conf_file }}"
    notify: Restart rsyslog

  - name: Make configuration directory
    file:
      path: /etc/rsyslog.d/
      mode: 0755
      state: directory

  - name: Configuring rsyslog forward rule
    template:
      src: forward_rule.conf.j2
      dest: "/etc/rsyslog.d/{{ rsyslog_forward_rule_name }}.conf"
    notify: Restart rsyslog
    when: not rsyslog_deploy_default_config

  - name: Configuring additional config files
    copy:
      src: "{{ item.value.src }}"
      dest: "/etc/rsyslog.d/{{ item.key }}"
      validate: "{{ item.value.validate | default(False) }}"
    notify: Restart rsyslog
    loop: "{{ rsyslog_rsyslog_d_files }}"
    when: item.value.state == "present"

  - name: Start and enable rsyslog
    service:
      name: "{{ rsyslog_service }}"
      state: started
      enabled: yes


